// TreeLock — ONE ADVISORY LOCK PER CHECKOUT, held by the commands that write the checkout's SHARED
// build products, so two of them can never run in one tree at once.
//
// Without it, two such commands corrupt each other's work:
//
//   1. **Two suites → `specs/.spec-tmp` → a FALSE RED.** Both runs stage their fragments under
//      the same per-spec scratch directory, so one deletes what the other is compiling and a lane
//      that is green reports `FAIL exit 1`.
//   2. **Two builds → `maxon-bin/.maxon/` → a FALSE SLOW, then a silent `exit 1`.** **A race that
//      manifests as SLOW is worse than one that manifests as WRONG, because slow gets attributed to
//      the change under test.**
//
// ============================================================================================
// WHAT IT LOCKS, AND WHO TAKES IT
// ============================================================================================
//
// **ONE lock per CHECKOUT, covering `build` AND the two harnesses together.** Not per output
// directory — a suite RUNS the binary a build REPLACES, so the two contend even though they write
// different directories, which is exactly the pairing `E6002`'s message already names as its likeliest
// cause. Not per machine either: every worktree carries its own `stdlib/`, `runtime/`, `bin/` and
// `.maxon/`, so worktrees must never block each other (that is the whole point of working in one).
//
// **The checkout is the one CONTAINING THE PATH THE COMMAND WRITES INTO** — the project directory, the
// spec directory, the scale corpus root — found by the same upward walk for `stdlib/` that locates the
// compiler's own source (`stdlibDirAbove`). A path with no checkout above it has nothing shared to
// guard, and takes no lock: `maxon build /tmp/scratch.maxon` is not a tree-level command.
//
// ⚠ **`stdlib/` ALONE IDENTIFIES THE CHECKOUT, AND ONE LOCK COVERS EVERY TIER IN IT.** `runtime/` is
// that directory's sibling under the same root, so the walk already lands on the tree that holds both;
// a second marker would only re-derive the same answer, and a second lock would split a guard whose
// whole point is that ONE command at a time writes the tree.
//
// Three commands take it (`Main`): `build <directory>` with no `--output=`, `spec-test`, `scale-test`.
// What they have in common is that they write the tree's own output directories; everything else — a
// one-off file build, an `--output=` build, `fmt`, `error-codes` — writes where the CALLER said and
// takes nothing. That distinction is what keeps the suite's thousands of child `build … --output=…`
// compiles free of it, and it is the ⛔ that would otherwise be a deadlock rather than a lock.
//
// `tests/spec-harness` runs `spec-test` at fixtures it copies under the host temp directory,
// outside any checkout, so those runs take nothing and never contend with each other or with a
// developer's own suite.
//
// ============================================================================================
// THE CLAIM FILE
// ============================================================================================
//
// The record is read and changed only by a command holding the claim file beside it, which it
// creates exclusively with a fresh token, so taking, taking over, refreshing and releasing the lock
// never interleave. A claim held by another command is waited on with a random backoff, for at most
// `ClaimWaitLimitMs`.
//
// A created claim is trusted only after a random settle and a re-read that still finds its token,
// and `changeRecordUnderClaim` re-reads it once more just before the record changes. A command
// removing a stale claim sets the file aside before it can read whose it is, so a fresh claim can
// vanish for a moment and be created again by a third command; the re-reads are what catch that.
//
// A claim nothing has touched for `ClaimStaleAfterSeconds` belonged to a command that ended while
// claiming. It is set aside under a `.removing-` name, deleted if it still holds the token that was
// judged stale, and put back if it does not.
//
// The record is written to a `.staged-` file and renamed over the lock, so a failed write never
// leaves a truncated record. A `.removing-`, `.probe-` or `.staged-` file its command left behind
// is swept once it is older than `ClaimStaleAfterSeconds`.
//
// ============================================================================================
// LIVENESS
// ============================================================================================
//
// A stale lock that outlives its holder blocks every later command forever, and a holder can die
// without releasing it: killed by hand, ended with its process tree when an MCP tool call reaches its
// timeout, or stopped by a panic, which runs no cleanup.
//
// So the record is REWRITTEN while its holder works (`TreeLockHold.touch`, throttled to one write
// every `TouchIntervalMs`), and its FILE MTIME is the heartbeat: a lock nothing has refreshed for
// `AbandonedAfterSeconds` is taken over, with a printed line saying so, even when its process still
// runs, because that holder has stopped making progress.
//
// A holder on this host is also probed by pid. One that has ended is taken over at once, and a
// record naming this command's own pid was left by a process that ended and whose id was reused.
//
// ⚠ **EVERY AGE COMPARES TWO MTIMES STAMPED BY ONE FILESYSTEM** — the file's against the held
// claim's or a fresh `.probe-` file's — never against this machine's clock. A checkout shared
// between hosts is stamped by one clock and judged by several, and a skew between them would break
// a live lock or keep a dead one.
//
// ============================================================================================
// THE RECORD IS ECHOED, NOT RE-DERIVED
// ============================================================================================
//
// A refusal QUOTES the record it found rather than reformatting parsed fields, so a field a reader
// does not know is still displayed, and a reader parses only the keys it acts on.
// The lines are plain `key=value` and may not be reordered for prettiness.

let LockFileName = ".maxon-tree.lock"
let ClaimFileSuffix = ".claim"
let ClockProbeInfix = ".probe-"
let StagedRecordInfix = ".staged-"
let SetAsideClaimInfix = ".removing-"
let SetAsideStampSeparator = "-"
let UnstampedAsideReason = "its name carries no time it was set aside at"

let LockFileWhat = "the tree lock"
let ClaimFileWhat = "the tree lock's claim file"
let ClockProbeWhat = "the tree lock's clock probe"
let LeftoverWhat = "the tree lock's leftover file"

let LeftInPlaceOutcome = "was left in place"
let NotRefreshedOutcome = "was not refreshed this time"

let PidField = "pid"
let TokenField = "token"
let SinceField = "sinceUnix"
let HeldField = "heldSeconds"
let ArgvField = "argv"
let HostField = "host"
let FieldSeparator = "="
let HostIdentitySeparator = "/"

#if os(Windows)
	let HostNameVariable = "COMPUTERNAME"
#endif

#if os(Linux)
	let KernelHostNamePath = "/proc/sys/kernel/hostname"
	let MachineIdPath = "/etc/machine-id"
	let DbusMachineIdPath = "/var/lib/dbus/machine-id"
#endif

let RecordLineSeparator = "\n"
let ArgvWordSeparator = " "

// The heartbeat must stay far below the abandonment window, so a slow phase or a busy disk never
// reads as a dead holder; the window must stay short, so a killed holder cannot wedge the tree.
let TouchIntervalMs = 5000
let RefreshRetryMs = 1000
let AbandonedAfterSeconds = 60
let RefreshWarningAfterSeconds = AbandonedAfterSeconds / 2
let MillisecondsPerSecond = 1000

let ClaimSettleMinMs = 10
let ClaimSettleMaxMs = 40
let ClaimBackoffMinMs = 20
let ClaimBackoffMaxMs = 120
let ClaimWaitLimitMs = 2000

// A claim is held for its settle and one record change, far under this; a window near that time
// would remove claims that are still live.
let ClaimStaleAfterSeconds = 10

// Whole seconds a lock has been held, or has gone untouched. A duration, not an instant: it is what
// the refusal prints and what the abandonment window compares against.
typealias LockSeconds = int(0 to u64.max)

type OwnedLock
	export let path as FilePath
	export let claimPath as FilePath
	export let token as String
	export let sinceUnix as UnixSeconds
	export let host as LockHost

	static function create(path FilePath, claimPath FilePath, token String, sinceUnix UnixSeconds, host LockHost) returns OwnedLock
		return Self{path: path, claimPath: claimPath, token: token, sinceUnix: sinceUnix, host: host}
	end 'create'
end 'OwnedLock'

type Acquisition
	export let lockPath as FilePath
	export let claimPath as FilePath
	export let claimToken as String
	export let host as LockHost

	static function create(lockPath FilePath, claimPath FilePath, claimToken String, host LockHost) returns Acquisition
		return Self{lockPath: lockPath, claimPath: claimPath, claimToken: claimToken, host: host}
	end 'create'
end 'Acquisition'

union LockHost
	known(identity String)
	unknown

	function recorded(identity String) returns bool
		return match self 'host'
			known(own) gives own == identity
			unknown gives false
		end 'host'
	end 'recorded'
end 'LockHost'

// A pid is probed only when a record's host identity equals this one (`holderOf`), so the identity
// names the machine AND its pid space: probing another machine's or container's pid would find it
// ended and take over a live lock. A part that cannot be read leaves the host unknown, which is
// never probed.
function thisLockHost() returns LockHost
	#if os(Windows)
		let hostName = try Process.environmentVariable(HostNameVariable) otherwise return LockHost.unknown
		return lockHostNamed([hostName, String.init(__Builtins.processNamespace())])
	#endif

	#if os(Linux)
		let kernelName = try firstNamedIn([KernelHostNamePath]) otherwise return LockHost.unknown
		let machineId = try firstNamedIn([MachineIdPath, DbusMachineIdPath]) otherwise return LockHost.unknown
		return lockHostNamed([kernelName, machineId, String.init(__Builtins.processNamespace())])
	#endif

	#if os(Macos)
		return lockHostNamed([String.init(__Builtins.processNamespace())])
	#endif

	#if os(Wasi)
		return LockHost.unknown
	#endif
end 'thisLockHost'

#if os(Linux)
	function firstNamedIn(locations StringArray) returns String throws AbsentError
		for location in locations 'eachLocation'
			let path = try FilePath.from(location) otherwise panic("TreeLock: '{location}' is not a valid path")

			let text = try File.readText(path) otherwise (e) 'unread'
				if faultOf(e.failure()) == FileFault.gone 'notHere'
					continue
				end 'notHere'

				throw AbsentError.absent
			end 'unread'

			if not text.trim().isEmpty() 'named'
				return text
			end 'named'
		end 'eachLocation'

		throw AbsentError.absent
	end 'firstNamedIn'
#endif

function lockHostNamed(parts StringArray) returns LockHost
	var identity = String.from(osCanonicalName(detectHostTarget().os))

	for part in parts 'eachPart'
		let trimmed = part.trim()

		if trimmed.isEmpty() 'namesNoHost'
			return LockHost.unknown
		end 'namesNoHost'

		identity.append("{HostIdentitySeparator}{trimmed}")
	end 'eachPart'

	return LockHost.known(identity)
end 'lockHostNamed'

union HeldTreeLock
	held(lock OwnedLock)
	none
end 'HeldTreeLock'

export type TreeLockHold
	var holding as HeldTreeLock
	var lastTouchMs as InstantMs
	var touchDelayMs as DurationMs
	var lastRefreshMs as InstantMs
	var refreshWarned = false

	export static function none() returns TreeLockHold
		return Self{holding: HeldTreeLock.none, lastTouchMs: 0, touchDelayMs: TouchIntervalMs, lastRefreshMs: 0}
	end 'none'

	// ⭐ Say the holder is still working. Cheap enough to call from anywhere that runs regularly — the
	// write is throttled to one every `TouchIntervalMs`.
	//
	// It is called from the places that are BOTH periodic and load-bearing: every compile phase
	// (`recordPhaseDelta`), every turn of the spec pool's dispatch loop, every scale rung. Those are the
	// sites at which "this process is still getting somewhere" is genuinely true, which is what the record
	// claims.
	//
	// ⚠ **THE OWNERSHIP TEST COMES FIRST, AND THAT ORDER IS THE COST.** Almost every caller of this holds
	// NO lock — every one of the suite's thousands of child compiles reaches `recordPhaseDelta` — so the
	// common path must be the cheap one: a match on `none`, and no clock read at all.
	export function touch()
		match self.holding 'holding'
			none then return
			held(lock) then self.touchHeld(lock)
		end 'holding'
	end 'touch'

	function touchHeld(lock OwnedLock)
		if Clock.elapsedMs(self.lastTouchMs) < self.touchDelayMs 'tooSoon'
			return
		end 'tooSoon'

		self.lastTouchMs = Clock.nowMs()

		let refresh = match takeClaim(lock.claimPath) 'claim'
			held(claimToken) gives refreshUnderClaim(lock, claimToken: claimToken)
			busy(untouchedSeconds) gives Refresh.contended(heldClaimReason(untouchedSeconds))
			contended(reason) gives Refresh.contended(reason)
			failed(reason) gives Refresh.failed(reason)
		end 'claim'

		match refresh 'refresh'
			refreshed then self.refreshed(lock)
			contended(reason) then self.contendedRefresh(lock, reason: reason)
			failed(reason) then self.failedRefresh(lock, reason: reason)
			foreign(found) then self.dropForeignHold(lock, found: found)
		end 'refresh'
	end 'touchHeld'

	function refreshed(lock OwnedLock)
		self.lastRefreshMs = Clock.nowMs()
		self.touchDelayMs = TouchIntervalMs

		if self.refreshWarned 'recovered'
			self.refreshWarned = false
			printError("note: {LockFileWhat} at {lock.path.toString()} is being refreshed again.\n")
		end 'recovered'
	end 'refreshed'

	function firstWarningSinceRefresh() returns bool
		if self.refreshWarned 'alreadyWarned'
			return false
		end 'alreadyWarned'

		self.refreshWarned = true
		return true
	end 'firstWarningSinceRefresh'

	function contendedRefresh(lock OwnedLock, reason String)
		self.touchDelayMs = RefreshRetryMs
		let unrefreshedSeconds = Clock.elapsedMs(self.lastRefreshMs) / MillisecondsPerSecond

		if unrefreshedSeconds < RefreshWarningAfterSeconds or not self.firstWarningSinceRefresh() 'stillFreshOrWarned'
			return
		end 'stillFreshOrWarned'

		printError("warning: the tree lock at {lock.path.toString()} has not been refreshed for {unrefreshedSeconds} s — {reason}, so this one could not take its claim file. Another command takes the lock over once nothing has refreshed it for {AbandonedAfterSeconds} s.\n")
	end 'contendedRefresh'

	function failedRefresh(lock OwnedLock, reason String)
		self.touchDelayMs = RefreshRetryMs

		if self.firstWarningSinceRefresh() 'firstFailure'
			warnUpkeep(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.refreshing, reason: reason)
		end 'firstFailure'
	end 'failedRefresh'

	// Give the lock up. A no-op for a hold that never took one, so every command may call it on the way
	// out without asking whether it holds anything.
	export function release()
		match self.holding 'holding'
			none then return
			held(lock) then self.releaseHeld(lock)
		end 'holding'
	end 'release'

	function releaseHeld(lock OwnedLock)
		self.holding = HeldTreeLock.none

		match takeClaim(lock.claimPath) 'claim'
			held(claimToken) then releaseUnderClaim(lock, claimToken: claimToken)
			busy(untouchedSeconds) then warnUpkeep(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.releasing, reason: "{heldClaimReason(untouchedSeconds)}, so the release could not take it")
			contended(reason) then warnUpkeep(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.releasing, reason: "{reason}, so the release could not take its claim file")
			failed(reason) then warnUpkeep(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.releasing, reason: reason)
		end 'claim'
	end 'releaseHeld'

	function dropForeignHold(lock OwnedLock, found ForeignRecord)
		self.holding = HeldTreeLock.none
		reportForeignRecord(lock, found: found, during: LockUpkeep.refreshing)
	end 'dropForeignHold'

	function take(lock OwnedLock)
		self.holding = HeldTreeLock.held(lock)
		self.lastTouchMs = Clock.nowMs()
		self.refreshWarned = false
		self.refreshed(lock)
	end 'take'
end 'TreeLockHold'

function refreshUnderClaim(lock OwnedLock, claimToken String) returns Refresh
	let refresh = match recordOwnership(lock.path, token: lock.token) 'owner'
		mine gives refreshOutcome(changeRecordUnderClaim(lock, claimToken: claimToken, change: RecordChange.rewrite(secondsSince(lock.sinceUnix))))
		another(record) gives Refresh.foreign(ForeignRecord.replaced(record))
		absent gives Refresh.foreign(ForeignRecord.removed)
		failed(reason) gives Refresh.failed(reason)
	end 'owner'

	releaseClaimOrWarn(lock.claimPath, token: claimToken)
	return refresh
end 'refreshUnderClaim'

function refreshOutcome(step LockStep) returns Refresh
	return match step 'step'
		done gives Refresh.refreshed
		failed(reason) gives Refresh.failed(reason)
	end 'step'
end 'refreshOutcome'

function releaseUnderClaim(lock OwnedLock, claimToken String)
	match recordOwnership(lock.path, token: lock.token) 'owner'
		mine then warnIfFailed(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.releasing, step: changeRecordUnderClaim(lock, claimToken: claimToken, change: RecordChange.removal))
		another(record) then reportForeignRecord(lock, found: ForeignRecord.replaced(record), during: LockUpkeep.releasing)
		absent then reportForeignRecord(lock, found: ForeignRecord.removed, during: LockUpkeep.releasing)
		failed(reason) then warnUpkeep(lock.path, upkeep: LockUpkeep.releasing, reason: reason)
	end 'owner'

	releaseClaimOrWarn(lock.claimPath, token: claimToken)
end 'releaseUnderClaim'

function changeRecordUnderClaim(lock OwnedLock, claimToken String, change RecordChange) returns LockStep
	match claimOwnership(lock.claimPath, token: claimToken, startedMs: Clock.nowMs()) 'claim'
		mine then break 'claim'
		another then return LockStep.failed("another command took over this command's claim on the lock before it could change the record")
		contended(reason) then return LockStep.failed(reason)
		failed(reason) then return LockStep.failed(reason)
	end 'claim'

	return match change 'change'
		rewrite(heldSeconds) gives writeRecord(lock, heldSeconds: heldSeconds)
		removal gives deleteRecord(lock.path)
	end 'change'
end 'changeRecordUnderClaim'

function reportForeignRecord(lock OwnedLock, found ForeignRecord, during LockUpkeep)
	printError("error: while {during.name} its tree lock, this command found that the lock at {lock.path.toString()} is no longer its own — another command broke it and took it while this one was still running, so two commands may now be writing this checkout's output directories. This command has dropped its hold and leaves the lock alone.\n")

	match found 'found'
		replaced(record) then printError("  It now says:\n{indentedRecord(record)}\n")
		removed then printError("  The lock file is gone.\n")
	end 'found'
end 'reportForeignRecord'

function warnIfFailed(lockPath FilePath, upkeep LockUpkeep, step LockStep)
	match step 'step'
		done then return
		failed(reason) then warnUpkeep(lockPath, upkeep: upkeep, reason: reason)
	end 'step'
end 'warnIfFailed'

function warnUpkeep(lockPath FilePath, upkeep LockUpkeep, reason String)
	let outcome = match upkeep 'upkeep'
		refreshing gives NotRefreshedOutcome
		releasing gives LeftInPlaceOutcome
	end 'upkeep'

	warnOutcome(LockFileWhat, path: lockPath, outcome: outcome, reason: reason, consequence: "The lock is treated as abandoned once nothing refreshes it for {AbandonedAfterSeconds} s.")
end 'warnUpkeep'

function warnOutcome(what String, path FilePath, outcome String, reason String, consequence String)
	printError("warning: {what} at {path.toString()} {outcome} — {reason}. {consequence}\n")
end 'warnOutcome'

enum LockUpkeep
	refreshing
	releasing
end 'LockUpkeep'

enum FileFault
	gone
	contended
	failed
end 'FileFault'

union FaultResponse
	gone
	retry
	exhausted(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'FaultResponse'

union FileText
	text(content String)
	fault(kind FileFault, reason String)
end 'FileText'

union FileStamp
	at(seconds UnixSeconds)
	fault(kind FileFault, reason String)
end 'FileStamp'

union FilesystemNow
	at(seconds UnixSeconds)
	fault(kind FileFault, reason String)
end 'FilesystemNow'

union ClockSource
	heldClaim(claimPath FilePath)
	measured(seconds UnixSeconds)
end 'ClockSource'

union AgedText
	present(text String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds)
	fault(kind FileFault, reason String)
end 'AgedText'

union RecordOwnership
	mine
	another(record String)
	absent
	failed(reason String)
end 'RecordOwnership'

union LockStep
	done
	failed(reason String)
end 'LockStep'

union RecordChange
	rewrite(heldSeconds LockSeconds)
	removal
end 'RecordChange'

union Refresh
	refreshed
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
	foreign(found ForeignRecord)
end 'Refresh'

union ClaimAttempt
	held(token String)
	busy(untouchedSeconds LockSeconds)
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'ClaimAttempt'

union ClaimStep
	held(token String)
	retry
	busy(untouchedSeconds LockSeconds)
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'ClaimStep'

union ClaimText
	text(content String)
	gone
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'ClaimText'

union ClaimOwnership
	mine
	another
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'ClaimOwnership'

union ClaimRemoval
	removed
	gone
	another
	contended(reason String, left FilePath)
	failed(reason String, left FilePath)
end 'ClaimRemoval'

union ClaimFileChange
	setAsideTo(aside FilePath)
	delete
end 'ClaimFileChange'

union ChangeAttempt
	done
	fault(kind FileFault, reason String)
end 'ChangeAttempt'

union ClaimChange
	done
	gone
	contended(reason String)
	failed(reason String)
end 'ClaimChange'

enum LockLeftover
	setAsideClaim
	clockProbe
	stagedRecord

	function prefix() returns String
		return match self 'leftover'
			setAsideClaim gives "{LockFileName}{ClaimFileSuffix}{SetAsideClaimInfix}"
			clockProbe gives "{LockFileName}{ClaimFileSuffix}{ClockProbeInfix}"
			stagedRecord gives "{LockFileName}{StagedRecordInfix}"
		end 'leftover'
	end 'prefix'
end 'LockLeftover'

type LeftoverSweep
	var swept = false

	static function pending() returns LeftoverSweep
		return Self{}
	end 'pending'

	function sweepOnce(claimPath FilePath, nowSeconds UnixSeconds)
		if self.swept 'alreadySwept'
			return
		end 'alreadySwept'

		self.swept = true
		sweepLeftovers(claimPath, nowSeconds: nowSeconds)
	end 'sweepOnce'
end 'LeftoverSweep'

union AcquireDecision
	takeFresh
	takeOver(warning String)
	busy(record String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, holder LeftoverOwner, liveness OwnerLiveness)
end 'AcquireDecision'

union ForeignRecord
	replaced(record String)
	removed
end 'ForeignRecord'

// Stopping answers `NothingRanExitCode`, the code `refuseIfStale` answers, because both mean the
// same thing to a caller reading only the number: nothing ran.
export function acquireTreeLock(operand FilePath, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	let lockPath = try lockPathFor(operand) otherwise 'noCheckout'
		// Nothing shared to guard. `operand` has no `stdlib/` above it, so no other command in any
		// tree writes what this one is about to write.
		return SucceededExit
	end 'noCheckout'

	let claimPath = claimPathFor(lockPath)
	let host = thisLockHost()

	return match takeClaim(claimPath) 'claim'
		held(claimToken) gives acquireUnderClaim(Acquisition.create(lockPath, claimPath: claimPath, claimToken: claimToken, host: host), into: into)
		busy(untouchedSeconds) gives reportClaimBusy(claimPath, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds)
		contended(reason) gives reportClaimContended(claimPath, reason: reason)
		failed(reason) gives reportLockFailure(reason)
	end 'claim'
end 'acquireTreeLock'

// The lock file for the checkout containing `operand`, or a throw when there is no checkout above it.
//
// `operand` is RESOLVED against the working directory first: `scale-test`'s corpus root is the
// relative `.scale-tmp` and a `build maxon-bin` names its project relatively too, and a relative
// single-component path has no parent to walk up from — so an unresolved one would silently answer
// "not in a checkout" for the very commands this lock exists for.
function lockPathFor(operand FilePath) returns FilePath throws CompileError
	let absolute = operand.resolve(Directory.currentPath())
	let stdlibDir = try stdlibDirAbove(absolute)
	let checkoutRoot = try stdlibDir.parent() otherwise throw CompileError.stdlibNotFound
	let name = try FilePath.from(LockFileName) otherwise panic("TreeLock: '{LockFileName}' is not a valid path component")
	return checkoutRoot.join(name)
end 'lockPathFor'

function claimPathFor(lockPath FilePath) returns FilePath
	return try FilePath.from("{lockPath.toString()}{ClaimFileSuffix}") otherwise panic("TreeLock: the path '{lockPath.toString()}' does not take the '{ClaimFileSuffix}' suffix")
end 'claimPathFor'

function leftoverPath(leftover LockLeftover, beside FilePath, unique String) returns FilePath
	let directory = try beside.parent() otherwise panic("TreeLock.leftoverPath: {beside.toString()} sits beside the tree lock at a checkout root, so it has a parent")
	let name = try FilePath.from("{leftover.prefix()}{unique}") otherwise panic("TreeLock.leftoverPath: '{leftover.prefix()}{unique}' is not a valid path component")
	return directory.join(name)
end 'leftoverPath'

function acquireUnderClaim(acquisition Acquisition, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	return match agedText(acquisition.lockPath, what: LockFileWhat, clock: ClockSource.heldClaim(acquisition.claimPath)) 'existing'
		present(text, untouchedSeconds) gives settleUnderClaim(acquisition, decision: decideOverExisting(acquisition.lockPath, record: text, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, host: acquisition.host), into: into)
		fault(kind, reason) gives settleRecordFaultUnderClaim(acquisition, kind: kind, reason: reason, into: into)
	end 'existing'
end 'acquireUnderClaim'

function settleRecordFaultUnderClaim(acquisition Acquisition, kind FileFault, reason String, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	return match kind 'kind'
		gone gives settleUnderClaim(acquisition, decision: AcquireDecision.takeFresh, into: into)
		contended or
			failed gives releaseClaimThenFail(acquisition, reason: reason)
	end 'kind'
end 'settleRecordFaultUnderClaim'

function settleUnderClaim(acquisition Acquisition, decision AcquireDecision, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	return match decision 'decision'
		takeFresh gives takeUnderClaim(acquisition, into: into)
		takeOver(warning) gives takeOverUnderClaim(acquisition, warning: warning, into: into)
		busy(record, untouchedSeconds, holder, liveness) gives releaseClaimThenReportBusy(acquisition, record: record, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, holder: holder, liveness: liveness)
	end 'decision'
end 'settleUnderClaim'

function releaseClaimThenFail(acquisition Acquisition, reason String) returns ExitCode
	releaseClaimOrWarn(acquisition.claimPath, token: acquisition.claimToken)
	return reportLockFailure(reason)
end 'releaseClaimThenFail'

function decideOverExisting(lockPath FilePath, record String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, host LockHost) returns AcquireDecision
	let holder = holderOf(record, host: host)

	if holderIsThisProcess(holder) 'reusedId'
		return AcquireDecision.takeOver("warning: taking over the tree lock at {lockPath.toString()} — it names {holderDescription(holder)}, which is this command's own process, so the command that took it has ended and its process id has been reused. It said:\n{indentedRecord(record)}\n")
	end 'reusedId'

	let liveness = livenessOfOwner(holder)

	return match liveness 'liveness'
		ownerGone gives AcquireDecision.takeOver("warning: taking over the tree lock at {lockPath.toString()} — the process that took it, {holderDescription(holder)}, has ended without releasing it. It said:\n{indentedRecord(record)}\n")
		ownerAlive or
			notOwned gives decideByHeartbeat(lockPath, record: record, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, holder: holder, liveness: liveness)
	end 'liveness'
end 'decideOverExisting'

function holderIsThisProcess(holder LeftoverOwner) returns bool
	return match holder 'holder'
		process(pid) gives pid == __Builtins.currentProcessId()
		notOwned gives false
	end 'holder'
end 'holderIsThisProcess'

function decideByHeartbeat(lockPath FilePath, record String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, holder LeftoverOwner, liveness OwnerLiveness) returns AcquireDecision
	if untouchedSeconds <= AbandonedAfterSeconds 'stillMoving'
		return AcquireDecision.busy(record, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, holder: holder, liveness: liveness)
	end 'stillMoving'

	return AcquireDecision.takeOver("warning: taking over an ABANDONED tree lock at {lockPath.toString()} — nothing has refreshed it for {untouchedSeconds} s (a live holder refreshes it every {TouchIntervalMs} ms), so the process that took it is gone or has stopped making progress. Is it still alive? {livenessLine(holder, liveness: liveness)}. It said:\n{indentedRecord(record)}\n")
end 'decideByHeartbeat'

function takeOverUnderClaim(acquisition Acquisition, warning String, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	printError(warning)
	return takeUnderClaim(acquisition, into: into)
end 'takeOverUnderClaim'

function takeUnderClaim(acquisition Acquisition, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	let lock = OwnedLock.create(acquisition.lockPath, claimPath: acquisition.claimPath, token: freshToken(), sinceUnix: WallClock.nowUnixSeconds(), host: acquisition.host)
	let written = changeRecordUnderClaim(lock, claimToken: acquisition.claimToken, change: RecordChange.rewrite(0))
	releaseClaimOrWarn(acquisition.claimPath, token: acquisition.claimToken)

	return match written 'written'
		done gives tookLock(lock, into: into)
		failed(reason) gives reportLockFailure(reason)
	end 'written'
end 'takeUnderClaim'

function tookLock(lock OwnedLock, into TreeLockHold) returns ExitCode
	into.take(lock)
	return SucceededExit
end 'tookLock'

function releaseClaimThenReportBusy(acquisition Acquisition, record String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, holder LeftoverOwner, liveness OwnerLiveness) returns ExitCode
	releaseClaimOrWarn(acquisition.claimPath, token: acquisition.claimToken)
	return reportBusy(acquisition.lockPath, record: record, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, holder: holder, liveness: liveness)
end 'releaseClaimThenReportBusy'

function agedText(path FilePath, what String, clock ClockSource) returns AgedText
	var text = ""

	match readClassified(path, what: what) 'text'
		text(content) then text = content
		fault(kind, reason) then return AgedText.fault(kind, reason: reason)
	end 'text'

	var stampSeconds = 0 as UnixSeconds

	match modifiedStamp(path, what: what) 'stamp'
		at(seconds) then stampSeconds = seconds
		fault(kind, reason) then return AgedText.fault(kind, reason: reason)
	end 'stamp'

	return match clockNow(clock) 'now'
		at(seconds) gives AgedText.present(text, untouchedSeconds: secondsBetween(stampSeconds, later: seconds))
		fault(kind, reason) gives AgedText.fault(FileFault.failed if kind == FileFault.gone else kind, reason: reason)
	end 'now'
end 'agedText'

function clockNow(clock ClockSource) returns FilesystemNow
	return match clock 'clock'
		heldClaim(claimPath) gives heldClaimStamp(claimPath)
		measured(seconds) gives FilesystemNow.at(seconds)
	end 'clock'
end 'clockNow'

function heldClaimStamp(claimPath FilePath) returns FilesystemNow
	return match modifiedStamp(claimPath, what: ClaimFileWhat) 'claimStamp'
		at(seconds) gives FilesystemNow.at(seconds)
		fault(kind, reason) gives FilesystemNow.fault(kind, reason: "{ClaimFileWhat} at {claimPath.toString()}, which this command holds, is gone" if kind == FileFault.gone else reason)
	end 'claimStamp'
end 'heldClaimStamp'

function readClassified(path FilePath, what String) returns FileText
	let content = try File.readText(path) otherwise (e) 'unread'
		return FileText.fault(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "could not read {what} at {path.toString()} ({e.name})")
	end 'unread'

	return FileText.text(content)
end 'readClassified'

function modifiedStamp(path FilePath, what String) returns FileStamp
	let info = try File.info(path) otherwise (e) 'noInfo'
		return FileStamp.fault(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "could not read the timestamp of {what} at {path.toString()} ({e.name})")
	end 'noInfo'

	return FileStamp.at(info.modifiedTime as UnixSeconds)
end 'modifiedStamp'

// On Windows a file whose delete is pending answers access denied until its last handle closes,
// which is contention. Elsewhere it is a real refusal, and must end in `reportLockFailure`.
#if os(Windows)
	let AccessDeniedFault = FileFault.contended
#else
	let AccessDeniedFault = FileFault.failed
#endif

function faultOf(failure FileFailure) returns FileFault
	return match failure 'failure'
		notFound gives FileFault.gone
		busy gives FileFault.contended
		accessDenied gives AccessDeniedFault
		alreadyExists gives FileFault.contended
		failed gives FileFault.failed
	end 'failure'
end 'faultOf'

function filesystemNow(claimPath FilePath) returns FilesystemNow
	let probe = leftoverPath(LockLeftover.clockProbe, beside: claimPath, unique: freshToken())

	try File.createText(probe, content: ClockProbeWhat) otherwise (e) 'unwritten'
		return FilesystemNow.fault(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "could not write {ClockProbeWhat} at {probe.toString()} ({e.name})")
	end 'unwritten'

	let stamp = modifiedStamp(probe, what: ClockProbeWhat)

	try File.delete(probe) otherwise (e) 'kept'
		warnOutcome(ClockProbeWhat, path: probe, outcome: LeftInPlaceOutcome, reason: "it could not be deleted ({e.name})", consequence: "Nothing reads it, so it may be deleted by hand.")
	end 'kept'

	return match stamp 'stamp'
		at(seconds) gives FilesystemNow.at(seconds)
		fault(kind, reason) gives FilesystemNow.fault(kind, reason: "{ClockProbeWhat} at {probe.toString()} was gone before its timestamp could be read" if kind == FileFault.gone else reason)
	end 'stamp'
end 'filesystemNow'

function recordOwnership(lockPath FilePath, token String) returns RecordOwnership
	return match readClassified(lockPath, what: LockFileWhat) 'record'
		text(content) gives ownershipOfRecord(content, token: token)
		fault(kind, reason) gives RecordOwnership.absent if kind == FileFault.gone else RecordOwnership.failed(reason)
	end 'record'
end 'recordOwnership'

function ownershipOfRecord(record String, token String) returns RecordOwnership
	let recordedToken = try fieldValue(record, key: TokenField) otherwise return RecordOwnership.another(record)
	return RecordOwnership.mine if recordedToken == token else RecordOwnership.another(record)
end 'ownershipOfRecord'

function writeRecord(lock OwnedLock, heldSeconds LockSeconds) returns LockStep
	let staged = leftoverPath(LockLeftover.stagedRecord, beside: lock.path, unique: lock.token)

	try File.writeText(staged, content: recordText(lock.token, sinceUnix: lock.sinceUnix, heldSeconds: heldSeconds, host: lock.host)) otherwise (e) 'unwritten'
		return LockStep.failed(withStagedRecordRemoved("could not write the tree lock's new record at {staged.toString()} ({e.name})", staged: staged))
	end 'unwritten'

	try File.rename(staged, to: lock.path) otherwise (e) 'unmoved'
		return LockStep.failed(withStagedRecordRemoved("could not move the tree lock's new record from {staged.toString()} to {lock.path.toString()} ({e.name})", staged: staged))
	end 'unmoved'

	return LockStep.done
end 'writeRecord'

function withStagedRecordRemoved(reason String, staged FilePath) returns String
	try File.delete(staged) otherwise (e) 'kept'
		if faultOf(e.failure()) == FileFault.gone 'neverWritten'
			return reason
		end 'neverWritten'

		return "{reason}, and the staged record could not be removed ({e.name})"
	end 'kept'

	return reason
end 'withStagedRecordRemoved'

function deleteRecord(lockPath FilePath) returns LockStep
	try File.delete(lockPath) otherwise (e) 'undeleted'
		return LockStep.failed("could not delete the tree lock at {lockPath.toString()} ({e.name})")
	end 'undeleted'

	return LockStep.done
end 'deleteRecord'

function takeClaim(claimPath FilePath) returns ClaimAttempt
	let startedMs = Clock.nowMs()
	var sweep = LeftoverSweep.pending()

	while true 'claiming'
		match claimStep(claimPath, startedMs: startedMs, sweep: sweep) 'step'
			held(token) then return ClaimAttempt.held(token)
			retry then continue
			busy(untouchedSeconds) then return ClaimAttempt.busy(untouchedSeconds)
			contended(reason) then return ClaimAttempt.contended(reason)
			failed(reason) then return ClaimAttempt.failed(reason)
		end 'step'
	end 'claiming'

	panic("TreeLock.takeClaim: the claiming loop leaves only by returning a step that is not a retry")
end 'takeClaim'

function claimStep(claimPath FilePath, startedMs InstantMs, sweep LeftoverSweep) returns ClaimStep
	let token = freshToken()

	try File.createText(claimPath, content: token) otherwise (e) 'notCreated'
		if e == FileWriteError.alreadyExists 'heldElsewhere'
			return claimHeldElsewhere(claimPath, startedMs: startedMs, sweep: sweep)
		end 'heldElsewhere'

		return claimStepAfter(respondTo(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "could not create {ClaimFileWhat} at {claimPath.toString()} ({e.name})", startedMs: startedMs))
	end 'notCreated'

	let settle = try randomMilliseconds(ClaimSettleMinMs, maxMs: ClaimSettleMaxMs) otherwise (e) 'noDelay'
		return abandonOwnClaim(claimPath, token: token, step: ClaimStep.failed("could not draw the random delay a claim waits before it is trusted ({e.name})"))
	end 'noDelay'

	sleep(settle)

	return match claimOwnership(claimPath, token: token, startedMs: startedMs) 'settled'
		mine gives ClaimStep.held(token)
		another gives ClaimStep.retry
		contended(reason) gives abandonOwnClaim(claimPath, token: token, step: ClaimStep.contended(reason))
		failed(reason) gives abandonOwnClaim(claimPath, token: token, step: ClaimStep.failed(reason))
	end 'settled'
end 'claimStep'

function abandonOwnClaim(claimPath FilePath, token String, step ClaimStep) returns ClaimStep
	releaseClaimOrWarn(claimPath, token: token)
	return step
end 'abandonOwnClaim'

function respondTo(fault FileFault, reason String, startedMs InstantMs) returns FaultResponse
	return match fault 'fault'
		gone gives FaultResponse.gone
		contended gives contend(startedMs, reason: reason)
		failed gives FaultResponse.failed(reason)
	end 'fault'
end 'respondTo'

function contend(startedMs InstantMs, reason String) returns FaultResponse
	if Clock.elapsedMs(startedMs) >= ClaimWaitLimitMs 'waitedEnough'
		return FaultResponse.exhausted("{reason}, and it kept failing that way for {ClaimWaitLimitMs} ms")
	end 'waitedEnough'

	return match backOff() 'backoff'
		done gives FaultResponse.retry
		failed(why) gives FaultResponse.failed(why)
	end 'backoff'
end 'contend'

function claimStepAfter(response FaultResponse) returns ClaimStep
	return match response 'response'
		gone or
			retry gives ClaimStep.retry
		exhausted(reason) gives ClaimStep.contended(reason)
		failed(reason) gives ClaimStep.failed(reason)
	end 'response'
end 'claimStepAfter'

function claimHeldElsewhere(claimPath FilePath, startedMs InstantMs, sweep LeftoverSweep) returns ClaimStep
	var nowSeconds = 0 as UnixSeconds

	match filesystemNow(claimPath) 'now'
		at(seconds) then nowSeconds = seconds
		fault(kind, reason) then return claimStepAfter(respondTo(kind, reason: reason, startedMs: startedMs))
	end 'now'

	sweep.sweepOnce(claimPath, nowSeconds: nowSeconds)

	return match agedText(claimPath, what: ClaimFileWhat, clock: ClockSource.measured(nowSeconds)) 'found'
		present(foundToken, untouchedSeconds) gives judgeLiveClaim(claimPath, foundToken: foundToken, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, startedMs: startedMs, nowSeconds: nowSeconds)
		fault(kind, reason) gives claimStepAfter(respondTo(kind, reason: reason, startedMs: startedMs))
	end 'found'
end 'claimHeldElsewhere'

function sweepLeftovers(claimPath FilePath, nowSeconds UnixSeconds)
	let directory = try claimPath.parent() otherwise panic("TreeLock.sweepLeftovers: the claim file at {claimPath.toString()} is a sibling of the lock file at a checkout root, so it has a parent")

	let entries = try Directory.list(directory) otherwise (e) 'unlisted'
		printError("warning: could not list {directory.toString()} to remove the tree lock's leftover files ({e.name}). They stay until a later command lists it.\n")
		return
	end 'unlisted'

	for entry in entries 'eachEntry'
		let leftover = try leftoverNamed(entry.filename()) otherwise continue
		sweepLeftover(entry, leftover: leftover, nowSeconds: nowSeconds)
	end 'eachEntry'
end 'sweepLeftovers'

function leftoverNamed(name String) returns LockLeftover throws AbsentError
	for leftover in LockLeftover.allCases 'eachLeftover'
		if name.startsWith(leftover.prefix()) 'thisKind'
			return leftover
		end 'thisKind'
	end 'eachLeftover'

	throw AbsentError.absent
end 'leftoverNamed'

function sweepLeftover(path FilePath, leftover LockLeftover, nowSeconds UnixSeconds)
	match leftoverStamp(path, leftover: leftover) 'stamp'
		at(seconds) then removeIfAbandoned(path, untouchedSeconds: secondsBetween(seconds, later: nowSeconds))
		fault(kind, reason) then warnUnswept(path, kind: kind, reason: reason)
	end 'stamp'
end 'sweepLeftover'

function leftoverStamp(path FilePath, leftover LockLeftover) returns FileStamp
	return match leftover 'leftover'
		setAsideClaim gives setAsideStamp(path)
		clockProbe or
			stagedRecord gives modifiedStamp(path, what: LeftoverWhat)
	end 'leftover'
end 'leftoverStamp'

// From the filesystem time written into the aside's name: a rename keeps the stale claim's own
// mtime, so its mtime would let a contender sweep the aside while its remover is still reading it.
function setAsideStamp(path FilePath) returns FileStamp
	let unique = path.filename().replaceFirst(LockLeftover.setAsideClaim.prefix(), with: "")
	let stampText = try unique.split(SetAsideStampSeparator).get(0) otherwise panic("TreeLock.setAsideStamp: a split of '{unique}' has a first part")
	let stamp = try int.fromString(stampText) otherwise 'unstamped'
		return FileStamp.fault(FileFault.failed, reason: UnstampedAsideReason)
	end 'unstamped'

	if stamp < 0 'beforeTheEpoch'
		return FileStamp.fault(FileFault.failed, reason: UnstampedAsideReason)
	end 'beforeTheEpoch'

	return FileStamp.at(stamp as UnixSeconds)
end 'setAsideStamp'

function removeIfAbandoned(path FilePath, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds)
	if untouchedSeconds <= ClaimStaleAfterSeconds 'stillInUse'
		return
	end 'stillInUse'

	try File.delete(path) otherwise (e) 'kept'
		warnUnswept(path, kind: faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "it could not be deleted ({e.name})")
		return
	end 'kept'

	printError("warning: removed a leftover tree lock file at {path.toString()} — nothing has touched it for {untouchedSeconds} s, and the command that made it lasts well under {ClaimStaleAfterSeconds} s, so it ended before it could remove the file.\n")
end 'removeIfAbandoned'

function warnUnswept(path FilePath, kind FileFault, reason String)
	if kind == FileFault.gone or kind == FileFault.contended 'removedOrInUseMeanwhile'
		return
	end 'removedOrInUseMeanwhile'

	warnOutcome(LeftoverWhat, path: path, outcome: LeftInPlaceOutcome, reason: reason, consequence: leftoverConsequence())
end 'warnUnswept'

function judgeLiveClaim(claimPath FilePath, foundToken String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, startedMs InstantMs, nowSeconds UnixSeconds) returns ClaimStep
	if untouchedSeconds > ClaimStaleAfterSeconds 'stale'
		return removeStaleClaim(claimPath, staleToken: foundToken, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds, startedMs: startedMs, nowSeconds: nowSeconds)
	end 'stale'

	if Clock.elapsedMs(startedMs) >= ClaimWaitLimitMs 'waitedEnough'
		return ClaimStep.busy(untouchedSeconds)
	end 'waitedEnough'

	return match backOff() 'backoff'
		done gives ClaimStep.retry
		failed(reason) gives ClaimStep.failed(reason)
	end 'backoff'
end 'judgeLiveClaim'

function backOff() returns LockStep
	let backoff = try randomMilliseconds(ClaimBackoffMinMs, maxMs: ClaimBackoffMaxMs) otherwise (e) 'noDelay'
		return LockStep.failed("could not draw the random delay a contended claim backs off by ({e.name})")
	end 'noDelay'

	sleep(backoff)
	return LockStep.done
end 'backOff'

function removeStaleClaim(claimPath FilePath, staleToken String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, startedMs InstantMs, nowSeconds UnixSeconds) returns ClaimStep
	return match removeClaimHolding(claimPath, token: staleToken, startedMs: startedMs, clock: ClockSource.measured(nowSeconds)) 'removal'
		removed gives staleClaimRemoved(claimPath, untouchedSeconds: untouchedSeconds)
		gone or
			another gives ClaimStep.retry
		contended(reason, _) gives ClaimStep.contended(reason)
		failed(reason, _) gives ClaimStep.failed(reason)
	end 'removal'
end 'removeStaleClaim'

function staleClaimRemoved(claimPath FilePath, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds) returns ClaimStep
	printError("warning: removed a stale tree lock claim file at {claimPath.toString()} — nothing has touched it for {untouchedSeconds} s, and a live claim lasts well under {ClaimStaleAfterSeconds} s, so the command that made it ended while it was claiming the lock.\n")
	return ClaimStep.retry
end 'staleClaimRemoved'

function removeClaimHolding(claimPath FilePath, token String, startedMs InstantMs, clock ClockSource) returns ClaimRemoval
	return match claimTextOf(claimPath, startedMs: startedMs) 'current'
		text(content) gives setAsideClaimHolding(claimPath, token: token, startedMs: startedMs, clock: clock) if content == token else ClaimRemoval.another
		gone gives ClaimRemoval.gone
		contended(reason) gives ClaimRemoval.contended(reason, left: claimPath)
		failed(reason) gives ClaimRemoval.failed(reason, left: claimPath)
	end 'current'
end 'removeClaimHolding'

function setAsideClaimHolding(claimPath FilePath, token String, startedMs InstantMs, clock ClockSource) returns ClaimRemoval
	var nowSeconds = 0 as UnixSeconds

	match clockNow(clock) 'now'
		at(seconds) then nowSeconds = seconds
		fault(kind, reason) then return claimRemovalAfter(kind, reason: reason, left: claimPath)
	end 'now'

	let aside = leftoverPath(LockLeftover.setAsideClaim, beside: claimPath, unique: "{nowSeconds}{SetAsideStampSeparator}{freshToken()}")

	return match retriedChange(claimPath, change: ClaimFileChange.setAsideTo(aside), startedMs: startedMs) 'setAside'
		done gives removeSetAsideClaim(claimPath, aside: aside, token: token, startedMs: startedMs)
		gone gives ClaimRemoval.gone
		contended(reason) gives ClaimRemoval.contended(reason, left: claimPath)
		failed(reason) gives ClaimRemoval.failed(reason, left: claimPath)
	end 'setAside'
end 'setAsideClaimHolding'

function claimRemovalAfter(kind FileFault, reason String, left FilePath) returns ClaimRemoval
	return match kind 'kind'
		gone gives ClaimRemoval.gone
		contended gives ClaimRemoval.contended(reason, left: left)
		failed gives ClaimRemoval.failed(reason, left: left)
	end 'kind'
end 'claimRemovalAfter'

function removeSetAsideClaim(claimPath FilePath, aside FilePath, token String, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimRemoval
	return match claimTextOf(aside, startedMs: startedMs) 'setAside'
		text(content) gives settleSetAsideClaim(claimPath, aside: aside, content: content, token: token, startedMs: startedMs)
		gone gives ClaimRemoval.gone
		contended(reason) gives discardUnreadAside(aside, step: ClaimRemoval.contended(reason, left: aside), startedMs: startedMs)
		failed(reason) gives discardUnreadAside(aside, step: ClaimRemoval.failed(reason, left: aside), startedMs: startedMs)
	end 'setAside'
end 'removeSetAsideClaim'

function discardUnreadAside(aside FilePath, step ClaimRemoval, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimRemoval
	return match retriedChange(aside, change: ClaimFileChange.delete, startedMs: startedMs) 'deletion'
		done or
			gone gives ClaimRemoval.removed
		contended or
			failed gives step
	end 'deletion'
end 'discardUnreadAside'

function settleSetAsideClaim(claimPath FilePath, aside FilePath, content String, token String, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimRemoval
	if content == token 'theJudgedClaim'
		deleteSetAsideClaim(aside, startedMs: startedMs)
		return ClaimRemoval.removed
	end 'theJudgedClaim'

	try File.createText(claimPath, content: content) otherwise (e) 'notRestored'
		if e != FileWriteError.alreadyExists 'notPutBack'
			printError("warning: the tree lock's claim file at {claimPath.toString()} held another command's claim, which this command set aside by mistake and could not put back ({e.name}). That command finds its claim gone and claims the lock again.\n")
		end 'notPutBack'
	end 'notRestored'

	deleteSetAsideClaim(aside, startedMs: startedMs)
	return ClaimRemoval.another
end 'settleSetAsideClaim'

function deleteSetAsideClaim(aside FilePath, startedMs InstantMs)
	match retriedChange(aside, change: ClaimFileChange.delete, startedMs: startedMs) 'deletion'
		done or
			gone then return
		contended(reason) then warnClaimLeft(aside, reason: reason)
		failed(reason) then warnClaimLeft(aside, reason: reason)
	end 'deletion'
end 'deleteSetAsideClaim'

function claimTextOf(path FilePath, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimText
	while true 'attempting'
		var response = FaultResponse.retry

		match readClassified(path, what: ClaimFileWhat) 'attempt'
			text(content) then return ClaimText.text(content)
			fault(kind, reason) then response = respondTo(kind, reason: reason, startedMs: startedMs)
		end 'attempt'

		match response 'response'
			gone then return ClaimText.gone
			retry then continue
			exhausted(reason) then return ClaimText.contended(reason)
			failed(reason) then return ClaimText.failed(reason)
		end 'response'
	end 'attempting'

	panic("TreeLock.claimTextOf: the loop leaves only by returning an answer")
end 'claimTextOf'

function retriedChange(path FilePath, change ClaimFileChange, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimChange
	while true 'attempting'
		var response = FaultResponse.retry

		match attemptedChange(path, change: change) 'attempt'
			done then return ClaimChange.done
			fault(kind, reason) then response = respondTo(kind, reason: reason, startedMs: startedMs)
		end 'attempt'

		match response 'response'
			gone then return ClaimChange.gone
			retry then continue
			exhausted(reason) then return ClaimChange.contended(reason)
			failed(reason) then return ClaimChange.failed(reason)
		end 'response'
	end 'attempting'

	panic("TreeLock.retriedChange: the loop leaves only by returning an answer")
end 'retriedChange'

function attemptedChange(path FilePath, change ClaimFileChange) returns ChangeAttempt
	return match change 'change'
		setAsideTo(aside) gives attemptedSetAside(path, aside: aside)
		delete gives attemptedDelete(path)
	end 'change'
end 'attemptedChange'

function attemptedSetAside(path FilePath, aside FilePath) returns ChangeAttempt
	try File.rename(path, to: aside) otherwise (e) 'unmoved'
		return ChangeAttempt.fault(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "could not set {ClaimFileWhat} at {path.toString()} aside ({e.name})")
	end 'unmoved'

	return ChangeAttempt.done
end 'attemptedSetAside'

function attemptedDelete(path FilePath) returns ChangeAttempt
	try File.delete(path) otherwise (e) 'undeleted'
		return ChangeAttempt.fault(faultOf(e.failure()), reason: "it could not be deleted ({e.name})")
	end 'undeleted'

	return ChangeAttempt.done
end 'attemptedDelete'

function claimOwnership(claimPath FilePath, token String, startedMs InstantMs) returns ClaimOwnership
	return match claimTextOf(claimPath, startedMs: startedMs) 'claim'
		text(content) gives ClaimOwnership.mine if content == token else ClaimOwnership.another
		gone gives ClaimOwnership.another
		contended(reason) gives ClaimOwnership.contended(reason)
		failed(reason) gives ClaimOwnership.failed(reason)
	end 'claim'
end 'claimOwnership'

function releaseClaimOrWarn(claimPath FilePath, token String)
	match removeClaimHolding(claimPath, token: token, startedMs: Clock.nowMs(), clock: ClockSource.heldClaim(claimPath)) 'removal'
		removed then return
		gone then printError("warning: the tree lock's claim file at {claimPath.toString()} no longer existed when this command came to release it, so there was nothing to remove.\n")
		another then printError("warning: the tree lock's claim file at {claimPath.toString()} was taken over by another command while this one held it, so it is left to that command.\n")
		contended(reason, left) then warnClaimLeft(left, reason: reason)
		failed(reason, left) then warnClaimLeft(left, reason: reason)
	end 'removal'
end 'releaseClaimOrWarn'

function heldClaimReason(untouchedSeconds LockSeconds) returns String
	return "another command has held its claim file for {untouchedSeconds} s"
end 'heldClaimReason'

function leftoverConsequence() returns String
	return "A command that finds the lock's claim file held removes it once nothing has touched it for {ClaimStaleAfterSeconds} s."
end 'leftoverConsequence'

function warnClaimLeft(path FilePath, reason String)
	warnOutcome(ClaimFileWhat, path: path, outcome: LeftInPlaceOutcome, reason: reason, consequence: leftoverConsequence())
end 'warnClaimLeft'

function randomMilliseconds(minMs Milliseconds, maxMs Milliseconds) returns Milliseconds throws RandomError
	let draw = try Random.below((maxMs - minMs + 1) as RandomBound)
	return minMs + draw as Milliseconds
end 'randomMilliseconds'

function reportClaimBusy(claimPath FilePath, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds) returns ExitCode
	printBusyHeadline("is claiming its tree lock")
	printError("  claim: {claimPath.toString()}\n")
	printError("  This command waited {ClaimWaitLimitMs} ms for the claim to be released; it was last touched {untouchedSeconds} s ago. A claim nothing has touched for {ClaimStaleAfterSeconds} s is removed automatically, with a line saying so.\n")
	return NothingRanExitCode
end 'reportClaimBusy'

function reportClaimContended(claimPath FilePath, reason String) returns ExitCode
	printBusyHeadline("is using its tree lock's claim file")
	printError("  claim: {claimPath.toString()}\n")
	printError("  {reason}.\n")
	return NothingRanExitCode
end 'reportClaimContended'

function printBusyHeadline(activity String)
	printError("error: this checkout is BUSY — another maxon command {activity}, and two of them in one tree corrupt each other's output directories. Nothing was run.\n")
end 'printBusyHeadline'

function reportLockFailure(reason String) returns ExitCode
	printError("error: the tree lock could not be taken — {reason}. The lock guards the shared output directories two commands would otherwise corrupt, so nothing was run.\n")
	printError("  If you are building inside an installed copy of Maxon, build from a directory you own instead.\n")
	return NothingRanExitCode
end 'reportLockFailure'

function freshToken() returns String
	return "{__Builtins.currentProcessId()}-{WallClock.nowUnixSeconds()}-{Clock.nowNanos()}"
end 'freshToken'

function recordText(token String, sinceUnix UnixSeconds, heldSeconds LockSeconds, host LockHost) returns String
	var text = StringBuilder.create()
	appendField(text, key: PidField, value: "{__Builtins.currentProcessId()}")
	appendField(text, key: TokenField, value: token)
	appendField(text, key: SinceField, value: "{sinceUnix}")
	appendField(text, key: HeldField, value: "{heldSeconds}")
	appendField(text, key: ArgvField, value: joinArgs())

	match host 'host'
		known(identity) then appendField(text, key: HostField, value: identity)
		unknown then break 'host'
	end 'host'

	return text.build()
end 'recordText'

function appendField(text StringBuilder, key String, value String)
	text.append("{key}{FieldSeparator}{value}{RecordLineSeparator}")
end 'appendField'

// This process's command line as one line. Newlines in an argument would forge a record field, so they
// are flattened to spaces — an argument holding one is not a thing this compiler's CLI accepts, and a
// record whose fields can be forged by an argument is not a record.
function joinArgs() returns String
	var words = StringArray.create()

	for arg in CommandLine.args() 'each'
		words.push(arg.replace(RecordLineSeparator, with: ArgvWordSeparator))
	end 'each'

	return joinedWith(words, separator: ArgvWordSeparator)
end 'joinArgs'

// The value of one `key=` line; a record that does not carry the key throws.
//
// `replaceFirst` off a line already known to START with the key, rather than `split("=")` and part 1 —
// which is the text between the FIRST and SECOND `=`, so any value containing one is silently
// truncated. `argv` routinely contains several (`--filter=…`, `--compiler=…`), and
// `CommandLine.optionValue` carries the scar from making exactly that mistake.
function fieldValue(text String, key String) returns String throws AbsentError
	let prefix = "{key}{FieldSeparator}"

	for line in text.split(RecordLineSeparator) 'eachLine'
		if line.startsWith(prefix) 'found'
			return line.replaceFirst(prefix, with: "")
		end 'found'
	end 'eachLine'

	throw AbsentError.absent
end 'fieldValue'

function secondsSince(stamp UnixSeconds) returns LockSeconds
	return secondsBetween(stamp, later: WallClock.nowUnixSeconds())
end 'secondsSince'

// Clamped at zero: a clock can step backwards (NTP, a VM resuming from a snapshot), and a backwards
// step must read as no time passed, which keeps a live lock rather than breaking it.
function secondsBetween(earlier UnixSeconds, later UnixSeconds) returns LockSeconds
	if later <= earlier 'notLater'
		return 0
	end 'notLater'

	return later - earlier
end 'secondsBetween'

function reportBusy(lockPath FilePath, record String, untouchedSeconds LockSeconds, holder LeftoverOwner, liveness OwnerLiveness) returns ExitCode
	printBusyHeadline("holds its tree lock")
	printError("  lock:  {lockPath.toString()}\n")
	printError("  held by:\n{indentedRecord(record)}\n")
	printError("  last progress: {untouchedSeconds} s ago (a live holder refreshes the record every {TouchIntervalMs} ms)\n")
	printError("  is it still alive? {livenessLine(holder, liveness: liveness)}\n")
	printError("  Wait for it to finish, or end that process. A holder that refreshes nothing for {AbandonedAfterSeconds} s, or a holder on this machine whose process has ended, is taken over automatically, with a line saying so.\n")
	return NothingRanExitCode
end 'reportBusy'

function livenessLine(holder LeftoverOwner, liveness OwnerLiveness) returns String
	return match liveness 'liveness'
		ownerAlive gives "yes — {holderDescription(holder)} is running"
		notOwned gives "the record names no process this host can probe, so only its heartbeat says"
		ownerGone panic("TreeLock.livenessLine: a holder that has ended is taken over by `decideOverExisting` before any refusal is reported")
	end 'liveness'
end 'livenessLine'

function holderOf(record String, host LockHost) returns LeftoverOwner
	let recordedHost = try fieldValue(record, key: HostField) otherwise return LeftoverOwner.notOwned

	if not host.recorded(recordedHost) 'anotherHost'
		return LeftoverOwner.notOwned
	end 'anotherHost'

	let pid = try fieldValue(record, key: PidField) otherwise return LeftoverOwner.notOwned
	return ownerProcessNamed(pid)
end 'holderOf'

function holderDescription(holder LeftoverOwner) returns String
	return match holder 'holder'
		process(pid) gives "process {pid}"
		notOwned gives "an unnamed process"
	end 'holder'
end 'holderDescription'

// The record, indented under the line that introduces it. Its own trailing newline is dropped so the
// caller's `\n` is the only one — a record ends with one, and two would put a blank line inside the
// message.
function indentedRecord(record String) returns String
	var out = StringBuilder.create()

	for line in record.split(RecordLineSeparator) 'eachLine'
		if line.isEmpty() 'blank'
			continue
		end 'blank'

		out.append("    {line}{RecordLineSeparator}")
	end 'eachLine'

	return out.build().trimEnd()
end 'indentedRecord'
